[64.360635, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[64.441437, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠧\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[64.52207, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[64.602873, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[64.68362, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠋\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[64.764426, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠙\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[64.844991, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[64.925765, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[65.007011, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[65.08773, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[65.169363, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[65.250503, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠧\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[65.330942, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[65.411632, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[65.442624, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m2\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[65.44316, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe input is a large array with active/inactive/pending users and ISO timestamps containing fractional seconds. I’ll test a jq filter that filters active users,\r\nparses the timestamp robustly after normalizing its fractional seconds, sorts by username, and uses explicit 2-space indentation.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app && jq --indent 2 'map(select(.status == \"active\") | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login | sub(\"\\\\.[0-9]+Z$\"; \r\n\"Z\") | fromdateiso8601 | strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")), role_count: (.roles | length), primary_role: (.roles[0] // null)}) | sort_by(.username)' users.json > \r\n/tmp/test_report.json && echo \"active_count=$(jq length /tmp/test_report.json)\" && jq 'map(select(.primary_role == null)) | length' /tmp/test_report.json && jq \r\n'.[0:3]' /tmp/test_report.json && echo '--- first/last usernames ---' && jq -r '.[0].username, .[-1].username' /tmp/test_report.json && echo '--- all usernames \r\nsorted? ---' && jq -r '.[].username' /tmp/test_report.json | sort -c && echo sorte"]
