[88.279922, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m5\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[88.280324, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe YAML-reconstructed command produced a byte-identical report, and the output passed structural checks. One validation query had a jq scoping error (not an \r\nissue with the generated report), so I’ll correct that test and finish the remaining checks.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app && jq -e --slurpfile report /app/active_users_report.json '\r\n  . as $src |\r\n  ([$src[] | select(.status == \"active\")] | length) as $active_count |\r\n  ($report[0] | length) == $active_count and\r\n  all($report[0][]; . as $out |\r\n    any($src[] | select(.status == \"active\" and .id == $out.user_id);\r\n      .username == $out.username and\r\n      .email == $out.email and\r\n      (.roles | length) == $out.role_count and\r\n      (if (.roles | length) == 0 then $out.primary_role == null else .roles[0] == $out.primary_role end) and\r\n      (.last_login[0:10]) == $out.last_login\r\n    )\r\n  )\r\n' /app/users.json >/dev/null && echo 'Cross-check against source passed' && echo '--- YAML keys ---' && yq -r 'keys | join(\",\")' /app/jq_args.yaml && echo '--- \r\nar"]
[88.280336, "o", "gs count ---' && yq -r '.args | length' /app/jq_args.yaml && echo '--- output indentation sample ---' && head -n 4 /app/active_users_report.json | cat -A && \r\necho '--- starts with JSON array, parses cleanly ---' && jq empty /app/active_users_report.json && echo valid-json\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[88.281075, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
